: 'Every login shell reads this file before its own .profile (cmd/sh/main.c),'
: 'so this is the one place a setting reaches every account, not just root.'
: 'TERM is guessed from the console only when nothing has already said what'
: 'the terminal is.  A window manager, telnetd and rlogind all know better'
: 'than /etc/console does: an mgr window on a machine that booted hrtty is'
: 'not an hrtty, and a login over the network is not this machine console at'
: 'all.  login(1) sets no TERM, so a console login still lands here.'
if /bin/test -z "$TERM"
then
	TERM=vt100
	if /bin/grep '^lrtty$' /etc/console >/dev/null 2>&1
	then
		TERM=lr
	fi
	if /bin/grep '^hrtty$' /etc/console >/dev/null 2>&1
	then
		TERM=hr
	fi
fi
export TERM
